{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - User - Authentication - One Okta Device Token Hash Across Many Accounts [table]",
	"Description": "Finds a single device token hash used to authenticate to several different accounts. One browser signing into three or more accounts is either a shared kiosk or one machine working through a list of stolen credentials.\n\nThreshold: 3 or more distinct accounts per device token hash. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_multiple_okta_user_authentication_events_with_same_device_token_hash/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta",
	"GUID": "da8352ea-e420-5137-a414-ab12d8e28d17",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Metadata": {
		"timeframe": null
	}
}